#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/quickstart.md:1
msgid "Quick Start (5 Minutes)"
msgstr "بدء سريع (5 دقائق)"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/quickstart.md:3
msgid ""
"The full path from nothing installed to a file on disk, using a free, no-"
"account provider — no login, no API key, no waiting on an approval email."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/quickstart.md:7
msgid "What you will do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/quickstart.md:9
msgid ""
"This walk-through takes you from an empty environment to a scene on disk in "
"four short steps, using a provider that needs no account so that nothing "
"stands between you and a first result. You install the package, run a search"
" that writes its findings to a GeoJSON file, download the best-ranked scene "
"from that file, and check the result. Afterwards the same workflow is "
"repeated in Python so you can see how the command line and the API map onto "
"each other: every command in the command-line interface has a counterpart on"
" the `PyGeoFetch` client, and they share the same query and download "
"options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/getting-started/quickstart.md:11
msgid ""
"Two ideas are worth holding on to as you read. First, search and download "
"are separate steps. A search only returns descriptions of scenes "
"(identifier, date, footprint, cloud cover and the list of files), which is "
"why it is fast and why you can run it as often as you like before deciding "
"what to download. Second, the GeoJSON results file is the hand-off between "
"the two steps, so you can search today, review the file, and download later "
"or on another machine. Once this works, move on to [Searching](../data-"
"access/search.md) to learn the filters, and to [Authentication](../data-"
"access/authentication.md) when you want providers that require a login."
msgstr ""

